  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the number of elements in the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8838;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is ______"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "112",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that if any set has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;elements then total number of subset is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p>So, total subset of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math>&nbsp;when set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;contains the element&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8838;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Total<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>112</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
